<div class="pd-column-grouper-documentation">

	<section id="overview">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Overview</h2>
		<p>
			<code>PDColumnGrouper</code> renders a single-select set of facet pills for the column groups of a
			<code>PDTable</code>. Selecting a facet shows only that group's columns (plus any ungrouped, pinned
			columns) and hides the rest &mdash; ideal for wide tables with dozens of columns where the column
			chooser dropdown becomes unwieldy.
		</p>
		<p>
			It is a transient view filter: it does not change, overwrite or persist the per-column visibility
			owned by the column chooser. The two compose &mdash; the chooser decides which columns are yours, the
			grouper decides which facet you are looking at right now.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="quick-start">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Quick Start</h2>
		<p>Declare groups with <code>PDColumnGroup</code>, then place a <code>PDColumnGrouper</code> anywhere and
			point it at the table's <code>@@ref</code>. Columns left outside a group are always shown.</p>
		<pre class="border rounded p-3 bg-light"><code>&lt;PDColumnGrouper TItem="Device" Table="_table" Variant="PDColumnGroupVariant.Segmented" ShowCounts="true" /&gt;

&lt;PDTable @@ref="_table" TItem="Device" ...&gt;

    &lt;PDColumn Field="x =&gt; x.Name" /&gt;            @* ungrouped - always shown *@

    &lt;PDColumnGroup Name="Meraki stats" Icon="fas fa-chart-bar" Ordinal="30"&gt;
        &lt;PDColumn Field="x =&gt; x.Latency" IsVisible="false" /&gt;
        &lt;PDColumn Field="x =&gt; x.Loss" IsVisible="false" /&gt;
    &lt;/PDColumnGroup&gt;

&lt;/PDTable&gt;</code></pre>
		<p class="text-muted small">
			Because the table is supplied via <code>@@ref</code> (assigned after the first render), call
			<code>StateHasChanged()</code> once in <code>OnAfterRender(firstRender)</code> on the host page so the
			grouper picks up the reference. After that it refreshes itself as columns register.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="variants">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Variants and options</h2>
		<p>
			Two visual styles are provided via <code>Variant</code>: <code>Segmented</code> (a joined control,
			the default) and <code>Pills</code> (separated, rounded pills). A per-group <code>Icon</code> and the
			<code>ShowCounts</code> flag are independent options that work with either variant. The active facet
			uses the Bootstrap primary colour and everything is overridable with CSS variables
			(<code>--pd-cg-active-bg</code>, <code>--pd-cg-idle-fg</code>, <code>--pd-cg-idle-border</code>, &hellip;),
			working in light and dark mode and on older Bootstrap versions.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="custom-styling">
		<h2 class="doc-section">Custom styling</h2>
		<p>
			Override the public <code>--pd-cg-*</code> variables on a class passed via <code>CssClass</code>. The
			component only ever <em>reads</em> these variables (falling back to its theme defaults), so a
			single-class override takes effect without any specificity battle. The demo's "Custom CSS" example uses:
		</p>
		<pre class="border rounded p-3 bg-light"><code>.pdcg-branded {
    --pd-cg-active-bg: #0d9488;
    --pd-cg-idle-fg: #0f766e;
    --pd-cg-idle-border: #99f6e4;
    --pd-cg-radius: 0.375rem;   /* squared-off pills */
}</code></pre>
		<p class="text-muted small mb-0">
			Variables: <code>--pd-cg-active-bg</code>, <code>--pd-cg-active-fg</code>, <code>--pd-cg-idle-fg</code>,
			<code>--pd-cg-idle-bg</code>, <code>--pd-cg-idle-border</code>, <code>--pd-cg-hover-bg</code>,
			<code>--pd-cg-count-bg</code>, <code>--pd-cg-active-count-bg</code>, <code>--pd-cg-radius</code>,
			<code>--pd-cg-segmented-radius</code>, <code>--pd-cg-gap</code>, <code>--pd-cg-font-size</code>. For
			structural changes use the <code>PillCssClass</code> / <code>ActivePillCssClass</code> /
			<code>TextCssClass</code> / <code>IconCssClass</code> hooks.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section id="parameters">
		<h2 class="doc-section">PDColumnGrouper parameters</h2>
		<table class="table table-sm doc-props-table">
			<thead>
				<tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>Table</code></td><td><code>PDTable&lt;TItem&gt;</code></td><td>The target table (supply its <code>@@ref</code>). Required.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Variant</code></td><td><code>PDColumnGroupVariant</code></td><td><code>Segmented</code> (default) or <code>Pills</code>.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ShowCounts</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>Show a column count badge on each facet. Default <code>false</code>.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ShowAllPill</code></td><td><code>bool</code></td><td>Show a leading "all columns" facet. Default <code>true</code>.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>AllText</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>Label for the "all columns" facet. Default <code>"All"</code>.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>AllIcon</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td>Optional icon for the "all columns" facet.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>CssClass</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td>Classes for the root element (e.g. <code>d-flex justify-content-center</code>).</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>PillCssClass</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td>Extra classes for every pill.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>ActivePillCssClass</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td>Extra classes for the active pill.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>TextCssClass</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td>Extra classes for the pill text.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>IconCssClass</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td>Extra classes for the pill icon.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</section>

	<section id="group-parameters">
		<h2 class="doc-section">PDColumnGroup parameters</h2>
		<table class="table table-sm doc-props-table">
			<thead>
				<tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>Name</code></td><td><code>string</code></td><td>Unique group name and pill label. Required.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Icon</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td>Optional icon CSS class for the pill.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Ordinal</code></td><td><code>int</code></td><td>Pill order, lower first. Default <code>1000</code>.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>Description</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td>Optional pill tooltip.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p class="text-muted small">
			An explicit <code>Group</code> on a <code>PDColumn</code> takes precedence over a wrapping
			<code>PDColumnGroup</code>.
		</p>

		<p>
			<strong>Declaring a group inline on columns.</strong> Instead of the <code>PDColumnGroup</code> wrapper you
			can set the group &mdash; and its pill metadata &mdash; directly on each <code>PDColumn</code> via
			<code>Group</code>, <code>GroupIcon</code>, <code>GroupOrdinal</code> and <code>GroupDescription</code>.
			This keeps the columns as direct children of the table (no wrapping element), which matters when another
			feature enumerates the table's columns &mdash; for example a <code>PDForm</code> whose fields are
			auto-generated from the column definitions. The icon, order and tooltip only need setting on one column of
			the group; the table de-duplicates by group name.
		</p>
		<pre class="border rounded p-3 bg-light"><code>&lt;PDColumn Field="x =&gt; x.Latency"
          Group="Meraki stats" GroupIcon="fas fa-chart-bar" GroupOrdinal="30" /&gt;
&lt;PDColumn Field="x =&gt; x.Loss" Group="Meraki stats" /&gt;</code></pre>
		<table class="table table-sm doc-props-table">
			<thead>
				<tr><th>PDColumn parameter</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>Group</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td>Group name / pill label the column belongs to. Empty means ungrouped (always shown).</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>GroupIcon</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td>Icon CSS class for the group's pill (set on one column of the group).</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>GroupOrdinal</code></td><td><code>int?</code></td><td>Pill order for the group; lower appears first.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>GroupDescription</code></td><td><code>string?</code></td><td>Tooltip shown when hovering the group's pill.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</section>

</div>
